@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` is exported from `src/index.ts`. It returns the merged document as a new value; neither argument is mutated and the result shares no structure with either.
+
+## Semantics (MergePatch algorithm, RFC 7386 §2)
+- If `patch` is not an object (scalar, `null`, or array), the result is a copy of `patch` (arrays replace wholesale; a top-level `null` yields `null`).
+- If `patch` is an object: a `target` that is not an object (scalar, array, null) is treated as `{}`. For each patch member: value `null` removes the member from the result (absent is fine); otherwise the member becomes `MergePatch(target[member], value)`, recursively. Members not mentioned are kept.
+- Consequently `null`s inside a patch object applied where the target has no object are dropped, not stored.
+- Only own members are read; `__proto__` is an ordinary key.
+- Values that are not JSON (undefined, NaN, functions, ...) in `patch` throw.
